module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.refusal_names_a_comparison_and_prints_neither_side

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data refusal_names_a_comparison_and_prints_neither_side: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "refusal_names_a_comparison_and_prints_neither_side" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a typed refusal names a threshold comparison as its cause and emits neither the threshold in force nor the measured quantity, so the reader cannot reproduce the verdict or size the gap** (INVALID STATE: a mechanism performs a comparison, refuses on it, and reports the comparison's NAME while discarding both of its operands.",

    "The refusal is fail-closed, typed, located and correct; what it cannot do is tell anyone how far over the line the subject was.",

    "**A refusal that names a budget and reports neither the budget in force nor the measured entry cannot distinguish over-by-a-percent from over-by-two-orders, and those prescribe different repairs.**",

    "The first is a tuning question, the second says the subject is the wrong shape entirely -- and a reader with only the cause string will pick between them by intuition.",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-09-07, measured while pricing a share-roster candidate: dispatch run 34088508298, job 101637093369 (`required-witnesses-floor`), refused with `REQUIRED-FLOOR REFUSAL cause=PureProducerShareWarmNotStored producer=v2.lens.common.outside_modeled_guarantee_join.witness_layer_decl_index -- the rostered producer evaluated but its value was refused by the cross-claim store: ByteBudgetExceeded`.",

    "The budget's authority is `CROSS_CLAIM_PURE_MEMO_BYTE_BUDGET` in `v1_interpreter`, whose own doc comment carries the figure and its derivation; the measured size is computed by `portable_value_size_bytes` over the total reification, AT PUBLICATION, which is precisely the moment the refusal is decided.",

    "So BOTH operands are in hand at the decision point and NEITHER survives into the log: the store retains only an `overflow` COUNT, and the refusal message carries the cause string alone.",

    "The per-producer `[floor-phase] phase=pure-producer-share-warm` line, which would have carried a disposition, was emitted with `disposition=Stored` for the two producers that stored and NOT AT ALL for the one that refused -- so the instrument that reports dispositions goes quiet on exactly the disposition a reader is looking for.",

    "HARM: the repair chosen after such a refusal is chosen without the one number that discriminates between the available repairs, and the cheapest wrong answer is always available -- raise the budget.",

    "Raising a budget to admit one oversized value is the absorbing fallback of DESIGN section 5 wearing the mechanism's own vocabulary, and a log that cannot show the magnitude is a log that cannot argue against it.",

    "WHY IT IS NOT `instrument_blind_spot_anti_correlated_with_severity`, filed the same night and genuinely adjacent: that class goes blind by DROPPING a subject whose observation never completed, so the record is ABSENT and reads as `never happened`.",

    "This class emits the record.",

    "It goes blind by PRINTING A COMPARISON WITH NEITHER SIDE, so the record is PRESENT and reads as `happened, magnitude unknowable`.",

    "The two also differ in what the fix is: there the mechanism must retain something it currently discards at a boundary it never reaches, here it must print two values it is already holding.",

    "WHY IT IS NOT `artifact_declares_a_threshold_it_is_not_measured_against`, which is the closer neighbour of the two: that class PRINTS a threshold and prints the WRONG one, so a consumer computes a well-formed population against a line nobody enforces.",

    "Here nothing wrong is printed -- nothing is printed.",

    "The two are the same defect at different arities and that neighbour's own amended trigger already names the general form one level up: a row from which the verdict cannot be recomputed is the defect, and line-versus-column-versus-nothing are ways to have it rather than distinct defects.",

    "This row is the ARITY-ZERO case, and it is filable separately because the neighbour's remedy -- emit the line ACTUALLY applied -- is satisfied vacuously by a refusal that emits no line at all.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable.",

    "The line stops, the refusal is typed and located and names the producer, so nothing proceeds on a wrong value; the containment is real and only the magnitude is lost.",

    "CEILING: 4, structurally impossible, and it is available today rather than aspirational.",

    "The refusal is CONSTRUCTED at the site that performed the comparison and therefore holds both operands; a refusal value carrying the threshold and the measured quantity as fields cannot be constructed without them, so the omission has no constructor.",

    "That is DESIGN section 5's correctness-by-construction rather than a check that the message was complete -- and the tell that today's shape is validation-shaped is that the cause is an authored `&'static str` chosen beside the comparison instead of derived from it.",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY: **the per-producer warm line is emitted for EVERY rostered producer including refused ones, carrying its disposition and the measured entry bytes against the budget in force** -- sufficient for a reader to reproduce the store's verdict from the log alone, demonstrated by a discriminating red on a fixture whose producer refuses and whose emitted line permits the refusal to be recomputed.",

    "A CONSEQUENCE FOR A NEIGHBOURING TYPE, RECORDED HERE SO THE NEXT LANE INHERITS IT RATHER THAN REDISCOVERING IT (this row does not author the change; `v2.workflow.floor_pure_producer_share` owns that type and a second lane editing it is how the conflict happens).",

    "`ShareRefusalVerdict` today has three arms -- `MeasuredServeAboveRecompute`, `NoMeasuredEffectOverItsConsumers`, `SupersededBySingleAuthorityRepair` -- and all three answer a COST question: is serving cheaper than recomputing.",

    "A `ByteBudgetExceeded` store refusal answers a CAPACITY question -- can this value be a shared value AT ALL -- and it is decided at publication, BEFORE any serving cost exists to compare.",

    "Recording it under a cost arm would be a MEANING FORK rather than a rounding error, and an INFLATING one: a capacity refusal filed as `MeasuredServeAboveRecompute` reads as `we measured and sharing lost` when the truth is `sharing was never available`, and the first ranks for a cost repair while the second ranks for a shape repair.",

    "Worse, `refused_row_carriers_transfer` treats `MeasuredServeAboveRecompute` as a measured cost that TRAVELS to other producers' consumers, so the fork would refuse unrelated candidates on a harm nobody observed.",

    "So that type needs a fourth arm for capacity, and until it exists a candidate refused this way is left PENDING rather than filed under a verdict that does not fit it.",

    "AND THE READING THAT MAKES THIS MORE THAN A LOGGING DEFECT: the specimen's refusal is the evidence that the value was never a sharing candidate.",

    "A value too large to be a shared value is a value that should not have been built to answer one question -- the producer materializes an entire corpus declaration index so that one declaration reference can be resolved -- so the missing magnitude was hiding a SHAPE finding behind a CAPACITY message.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
